Libft

This project has been created as part of the 42 curriculum by <ajenah>.

Description

Libft is a custom C library containing reimplementations of standard C library functions, useful utility functions, and linked-list manipulation utilities.

The goal of this project is to gain a deeper understanding of C programming fundamentals, heap memory allocation, and the inner mechanics of system functions.

Instructions

Compilation

Compile the static library using make:

make


Makefile Rules

make — Compiles mandatory library functions

make clean — Removes object files (.o)

make fclean — Removes object files and libft.a

make re — Recompiles the library from scratch

The resulting archive is generated as libft.a.

Usage

Include the main header in your C files:

#include "libft.h"


Compile your program by linking the library:

cc main.c -L. -lft -o my_program


Library Contents

Libc Functions: Custom implementations of standard C library routines (e.g., ft_strlen, ft_memcpy, ft_atoi).

Additional Functions: Useful string manipulation, memory management, and file descriptor output utilities.

Linked Lists: Functions designed to allocate, manipulate, iterate over, and clear node-based data structures.

